<title>FRANCE: Analyst sees one pct drop in EU 97/98 grain output.</title>
<headline>Analyst sees one pct drop in EU 97/98 grain output.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-04-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>French grain analyst Strategie Grains predicted on Tuesday that 1997/98 grain production in the European Union may drop by one percent to 202.6 million tonnes from 204.2 million in 1996/97, mostly the result of lower yields.</p>
<p>Last month Strategie Grains said 1997/98 grain output would reach 206.5 million tonnes.</p>
<p>In its monthly report for April, the analyst also said it had cut its estimate for 1997 grain sowings by 200,000 hectares to 37.8 million hectares. This would still represent a rise of three percent over 1996 sowings of 36.8 million hectares.</p>
<p>It put grain yields at 5.4 tonnes per hectare, down three percent over 1996/97.</p>
</text>
